      "leftHeadline": "A Moral and Patriotic Duty to Protest",
      "leftText": "Anti-war activists argued that the war was immoral, undemocratic, and was destroying both Vietnamese lives and American youth through a rigged class-based draft system.",
      "rightHeadline": "Unpatriotic Dissent and Lawlessness",
      "rightText": "Conservative hawks and Nixon supporters claimed that campus protesters were draft-dodging radicals who actively aided the communist enemy by destroying national unity.",
